{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EntityEvent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Protocol","role":"symbol","title":"EntityEvent","modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Observers.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Observers.swift#L58"},"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","externalID":"s:11WorldModule11EntityEventP"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"A type that describes something that happens to a particular entity, which its observers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"respond to at once.","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityEvent","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use an entity event when one part of a program needs to tell an entity that something"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"happened to it, and other parts need to respond right away: a barrel is hit, a button is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"clicked. Declare the event as a type that conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntityEvent"},{"type":"text","text":", register observers with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/observe(_:on:perform:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/observe(_:perform:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and trigger it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/trigger(_:on:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". The observers run before "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trigger(_:on:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following example despawns a barrel when it explodes:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct Explode: EntityEvent { var radius: Double }","","var world = World()","let barrel = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Barrel\"))","world.observe(Explode.self, on: barrel) { world, trigger in","    world.despawn(trigger.entity)","}","","world.trigger(Explode(radius: 3), on: barrel)","print(world.contains(barrel))","\/\/ Prints \"false\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An entity event differs from an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Event","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which waits in a queue until systems read it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Propagating Up the Hierarchy","anchor":"Propagating-Up-the-Hierarchy","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event whose "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EntityEvent\/propagates","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" property is "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" moves on to the entity’s parent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/ChildOf","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") after the entity’s observers run, then to that entity’s parent, and so on up to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the root. The following example lets a panel respond to clicks on any of its buttons:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct Clicked: EntityEvent {","    static var propagates: Bool { true }","}","struct ClickLog: Resource { var entries: [String] = [] }","","var world = World()","world.resources.insert(ClickLog())","let panel = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Panel\"))","let button = world.spawn(Name(value: \"OK\"))","try world.addChild(button, to: panel)","","world.observe(Clicked.self, on: panel) { world, trigger in","    let name = world[Name.self, of: trigger.originalEntity].value","    world.resources[ClickLog.self].entries.append(\"Panel saw a click on \\(name)\")","}","","world.trigger(Clicked(), on: button)","print(world.resources[ClickLog.self].entries)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Panel saw a click on OK\"]\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An observer can stop an event from going further by setting the trigger’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Trigger\/propagates","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" property to "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/entityevent"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EntityEvent\/propagates"],"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties","generated":true}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Trigger"],"title":"Reacting to Changes with Hooks and Observers","anchor":"Reacting-to-Changes-with-Hooks-and-Observers","generated":true}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\